{"id":114273,"title":"Constructing Material Interfaces from Data Sets with Volume-Fraction Information","url":"https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc739076/?q=marching cubes","final_url":"https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc739076/m2/1/high_res_d/791509.pdf","year":null,"kind":"link","source":"os:digital.library.unt.edu","doi":null,"arxiv":null,"sha256":"5228e5755f11f248ab572e1de81ab6e8d485856749ac2af907f844bea70a9ce3","ctype":"application/pdf","text_src":"url","fetched_at":1793236067.105308,"text_chars":29141,"abstract":"We present a new algorithm for material boundary interface reconstruction from data sets containing volume fractions. We transform the reconstruction problem to a problem that analyzes the dual data set, where each vertex in the dual mesh has an associated barycentric coordinate tuple that represents the fraction of each material present. After constructing the dual tetrahedral mesh from the original mesh, we construct material boundaries by mapping a tetrahedron into barycentric space and calculating the intersections with Voronoi cells in barycentric space. These intersections are mapped back to the original physical space and triangulated to form the boundary surface approximation. This algorithm can be applied to any grid structure and can treat any number of materials per element/vertex.","file":null,"marks":[],"links":["https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc739076/m2/1/high_res_d/791509.pdf","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc739076/?q=marching cubes","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc739076/?q=marching cubes ambiguity","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc739076/?q=marching tetrahedra","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc739076/?q=dual marching cubes","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc739076/?q=marching cubes algorithm","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc739076/?q=lorensen cline marching cubes","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc739076/?q=marching tetrahedra algorithm","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc739076/?q=marching cubes edge completeness","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc739076/?q=marching squares algorithm","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc739076/?q=nielson dual marching cubes","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc739076/?q=barycentric interpolation tetrahedra","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc739076/?q=tetrahedral normal calculation","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc739076/?q=hexahedral normal calculation","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc739076/?q=manifold dual marching cubes","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc739076/?q=marching tetrahedra reconstruction","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc739076/?q=marching tetrahedra 3","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc739076/?q=dual marching cubes vertex processing","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc739076/?q=case-based marching tetrahedra"],"cited_by":[{"path":"940-marching-tetrahedrons-algorithm.md","name":"Marching Tetrahedrons Algorithm","k":2},{"path":"9849-barycentric-mapping-for-material-interfaces.md","name":"Barycentric Mapping for Material Interfaces","k":1},{"path":"9890-barycentric-mapping-for-material-interfaces-2d-triangular-gr.md","name":"Barycentric Mapping for Material Interfaces (2D Triangular Grids)","k":1},{"path":"9851-adjustable-center-point-for-voronoi-partitioning.md","name":"Adjustable Center Point for Voronoi Partitioning","k":1}]}